--TEST--
hovering the `@key` step of a `propertyPath<T>` literal shows the type of an array's key and names the array property it follows — `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Post {
    public string $title = "Hello";
    public array<string> $keywords = [];
}
class Grid {
    public static function sortBy(propertyPath<Post> $column): string {
        return $column as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::sortBy("keywords.@k<|>ey");
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
int|string
```

The key of an element of `$keywords`.
